"\n","The results indicate that these variables exhibit very weak correlations with weekly sales. For example, unemployment and CPI show small negative correlations, while fuel price and temperature show near-zero correlations with sales.\n","\n","This suggests that macroeconomic indicators have limited short-term influence on weekly store revenue in this dataset. Retail demand appears to be driven more strongly by historical sales patterns and seasonal effects rather than external economic variables.\n","\n","These findings support the importance of time-series features such as lag values and rolling averages in forecasting models.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"k6JamQnaQGwy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Linear Regression Forecast Evaluation\n","\n","The model successfully captures the general sales range and overall fluctuations.\n","\n","However, predictions appear smoother than the actual sales values.\n","\n","The model struggles to capture sharp peaks and sudden changes in demand.\n","\n","This suggests that linear regression is too simple to model complex retail sales patterns\n"],"metadata":{"id":"QHlv38MuD1-T"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Model Comparison\n","\n","Two models were evaluated for forecasting Walmart sales:\n","\n","Linear Regression\n","\n","Random Forest Regressor\n","\n","The evaluation metric used was Mean Absolute Error (MAE).\n","\n","Results:\n","\n","\n","Linear Regression MAE: 43,469\n","\n","Random Forest MAE: 39,192\n","\n","Random Forest achieved the lowest error because it can capture nonlinear relationships between lag features and external variables.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"t24KFrsqGdUI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Feature Importance Analysis\n","\n","The Random Forest model indicates that the 4-week rolling mean of sales is by far the most influential feature, accounting for approximately 94% of the model's predictive power. This suggests that short-term demand trends strongly influence future sales.\n","\n","Individual lag features such as lag_1, lag_4, and lag_12 contribute additional predictive signal but are less influential because the rolling mean already captures recent sales dynamics.\n","\n","External variables including temperature, CPI, fuel prices, and unemployment exhibit relatively low importance, indicating that historical demand patterns are far more predictive of future retail sales than macroeconomic indicators in this dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"DWyIeywzJXQ_"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Future Sales Forecast (Next 12 Weeks)\n","\n","After training the forecasting model, future sales were predicted for the next 12 weeks using the most recent feature values. The forecast was generated iteratively by updating lag features with each predicted value.\n","\n","The resulting forecast indicates relatively stable weekly demand, with predicted sales remaining close to the recent historical average. This behavior is expected because the model identified the 4-week rolling average of sales as the most influential feature, indicating that recent demand trends strongly influence near-future sales.\n","\n","Overall, the forecast suggests no significant upward or downward trend in the short term, and weekly demand is expected to remain consistent with recent sales patterns."],"metadata":{"id":"LL1Ik-huQSZR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Future Sales Forecast (Next 12 Weeks)\n","\n","After training the forecasting model, future sales were predicted for the next 12 weeks using the most recent feature values. The forecast was generated iteratively by updating lag features with each predicted value.\n","\n","The resulting forecast indicates relatively stable weekly demand, with predicted sales remaining close to the recent historical average. This behavior is expected because the model identified the 4-week rolling average of sales as the most influential feature, indicating that recent demand trends strongly influence near-future sales.\n","\n","Overall, the forecast suggests no significant upward or downward trend in the short term, and weekly demand is expected to remain consistent with recent sales patterns."],"metadata":{"id":"adMTiTZBQVzF"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["XGBoost Model\n","\n","To further improve forecasting performance, an additional model was trained using Extreme Gradient Boosting (XGBoost). XGBoost is a powerful ensemble learning algorithm that builds models sequentially, where each new tree attempts to correct the prediction errors of the previous trees. This approach often allows the model to capture more complex nonlinear relationships between features.\n","\n","The model was trained using lag features, rolling averages, and external variables such as temperature, fuel price, CPI, and unemployment. Hyperparameters such as the number of estimators, learning rate, and tree depth were tuned to improve model performance and reduce forecasting error.\n","\n","After tuning the model, predictions were generated for the test dataset and compared with the actual weekly sales values. The XGBoost model successfully captured the general trend and fluctuations in the data.\n","\n","The tuned XGBoost model achieved a Mean Absolute Error (MAE) of approximately 39,857, which represents a small improvement over the initial configuration of the model."],"metadata":{"id":"Xw6WxPKwQfOZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Model Performance Comparison\n","\n","Three machine learning models were evaluated for forecasting Walmart weekly sales:\n","\n","Model\tMAE\n","Linear Regression\t43,469\n","Random Forest\t39,192\n","XGBoost (Tuned)\t39,857\n","\n","The results show that Random Forest achieved the lowest forecasting error, making it the best-performing model for this dataset.\n","\n","Although XGBoost is a more advanced boosting algorithm and performed well after tuning, the Random Forest model slightly outperformed it. This outcome suggests that the dataset is strongly influenced by recent sales trends 